    {
      "id": "claim_70cbf6803ceb469a9ff9a95f89aab9b9",
      "statement": "The Trusted Actions OpenAPI document declares a single global security scheme, ocm_jwt, an HTTP bearer JWT validated against the Red Hat SSO JWKS endpoint with caller identity taken from the username claim (falling back to preferred_username); the /health endpoint is served outside the OpenAPI-defined contract directly by cmd/server/main.go, registered before the /api/v0/trusted-actions route group, and is explicitly marked public (Public(\"^/health$\")) to the conditionally-applied OCM authentication handler so it works without a token when auth is enabled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/cmd/server/main.go#L367-L372",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce590c86e0bcb5e22cb7580c40c3c695e90ab1e234c21d5dc6a68425a1dadcc5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/cmd/server/main.go#L394-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:673c446d7602721c16e6df68fe7226149d12e8c3abd2dfe056cac63acffe25b3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/openapi/components/securitySchemes/ocm_jwt.yaml",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:5f507c68d55a5d3aacf5eb324e46de27fe6bd0b0980c4e8271f712c7357200fe"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/openapi/openapi.yaml#L57-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77337e2b5eb7792d4c6573435a1f0e01bc1472d696c5a2a1b557711f71c9048a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_35fc445fb0954e7192e6b07d98cb56ff",
      "statement": "As of the current OpenAPI document, no path file (including catalog.yaml and {action}.yaml) declares a security: [] override; the ocm_jwt scheme is applied globally in openapi.yaml with no per-path exceptions, so every documented route under /api/v0/trusted-actions, including catalog (GET /) and describe (GET /{action}), requires the bearer token. This matches the server's actual enforcement: cmd/server/main.go mounts the whole /api/v0/trusted-actions sub-tree as one chi route group wrapped in authentication, audit-logging, and authorization middleware before any handler in that group runs, so there is no current authn-vs-spec mismatch on catalog/describe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/cmd/server/main.go#L378-L386",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab207d57e290faf8f85e6b007b7c6b933249b30eebb714e71d30dc7cc87627ac:"
        },
        {
